# Cursor

Read @docs/agent-rules.md before your first edit in this repo. It is the single source of truth for domain
naming, style, security, the attempt-lifecycle invariants, quality, git, and when to ask.

Do not restate those rules here. If this file and `docs/agent-rules.md` disagree, `docs/agent-rules.md`
wins.

`/prd` and `/implement-prd` are Claude Code skills and do not exist in Cursor. Nothing in the rules asks you
to start one anyway — they run only when the developer invokes them. The git absolutes in that file have no
mechanical backstop here; they bind you anyway.
